course: dictionary
lesson: 12668
title: Swelling and stretching
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To distend means to swell out or stretch because something is pushing from inside. Think of a balloon filling with air: it gets bigger and rounder. «The balloon began to distend as Sam blew more air into it.» The air inside pushes outwards, so the balloon swells.
explain: The word is also used for bodies. «After the big meal, his stomach was distended and he could not move.» His stomach did not just get bigger by itself: food and gas pushed it outwards. When you read a word like this, ask what is pressing from inside.
explain: Distended can also be an adjective, which describes a thing. A distended stomach is one that is swollen and puffed out. Distend is the verb (the action), and distended is the describing word.
fact: To distend means to swell out or stretch because of pressure from inside.
fact: «Distended» is an adjective, meaning swollen and puffed out.
fact: Verb forms: distend, distends, distended, distending.
fact: In science and health, a stomach or balloon distends when it is filled with gas or liquid.
fact: In news about hunger, a child's belly may look distended because the child is badly fed, so the word can show a serious problem.
exercise: In «The balloon began to distend as Sam blew more air into it», what does distend mean? | To shrink and go flat | *To swell out and stretch | To make a loud bang | To float slowly up to the sky
exercise: «After the big meal, his stomach was distended.» Which word is closest in meaning to distend? | Shrink | *Puff out | Cool down | Empty
exercise: Tom's stomach began to distend after the fizzy drink. What is causing it to swell? | Loud music | Sunlight | *Gas inside | Cold air
test: «The pipe began to distend under the water's pressure.» What is pushing from inside the pipe? | Dust | *The water pressing inside it | Sunshine | Wind blowing outside
test: «Mia's tummy looked distended after the feast.» What kind of word is distended here? | Verb | Adverb | Noun | *Adjective
exam: «The bag was so full of air that its sides began to distend.» What does distend mean here? | Tear open | *Swell out and stretch | Go quiet | Dry out
